# An UPPERCASE receiver that names no module, record or ADT is a typo, not a
# namespace. The walker used to strip the qualifier and dispatch on the bare
# method name, so `Maths.sqrt(4.0)` quietly answered 2.0 via the global `sqrt`
# while BEAM rejected it. Both backends now refuse it, identically.
# kex: no-check
# kex: run-beam

main do
  IO.printLine("before")
  IO.inspect(Maths.sqrt(4.0))
end
